# Force LF on checkout, on every platform.
#
# Git stores these blobs as LF, but a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true — the default from the
# Git for Windows installer — writes CRLF into the working tree. Prettier is configured for LF, so
# `just check` then fails on every file in the repository for a reviewer who did nothing wrong.
# `eol=lf` makes the working tree match what is stored.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Kept out of the text pipeline entirely; these are gitignored today, but line-ending translation
# on a Parquet file would corrupt it rather than fail loudly.
*.parquet binary
*.duckdb  binary
*.wasm    binary
